 of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"6.5","spread":"16.83"}]}]}]},{"type":"PRIMARY","title":"Number of RBC Transfusion Instances","populationDescription":"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"RBC transfusion instances","timeFrame":"Baseline up to Week 169","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Danicopan","description":"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\[mg\\] 3 times daily \\[TID\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"3.4","spread":"8.00"}]}]}]},{"type":"PRIMARY","title":"Change From Baseline in PNH Clone Size at Week 25","description":"The PNH clone size refers to the percentage of PNH-affected cells versus normal cells within the total cell population. Change from Baseline = PNH clone size at Week 25 - Baseline PNH clone size. Baseline was the baseline value from the primary Study ACH471-100.","populationDescription":"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants with both baseline and the postbaseline assessments for PNH clone size.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"percentage of the total cell population","timeFrame":"Baseline, Week 2