 who was exposed to the study drug), important medical event or reaction. The intensity of an AE was graded according to the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events (CTCAE) Adverse Event Severity Grading Table. A summary of all Serious Adverse Events and Other Adverse Events (nonserious) regardless of causality is located in the 'Reported Adverse Events' Section.","populationDescription":"Safety analysis set included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose of danicopan.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"NUMBER","unitOfMeasure":"participants","timeFrame":"Baseline up to 4.5 years","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Danicopan","description":"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\[mg\\] 3 times daily \\[TID\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Any TEAEs","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8"}]}]},{"title":"SAEs","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"3"}]}]},{"title":"TEAE Grade 3","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"2"}]}]},{"title":"TEAE Grade 4","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"}]}]},{"title":"AE leading to discontinuation","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in LDH Level at Weeks 49 and 169","description":"Change from Baseline = Serum LDH levels at specified postbaseline visit - Baseline Serum LDH levels. Baseline was the baseline value from the primary Study ACH471-100.","populationDescription":"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall n